There's nothing wrong with tricks, but when they make the game too 
easy to win, they need to be weakened.

Won again tonight.  Samurai, this time.  No polypiling, just the wand
of wishing and the ring of conflict.  It's getting to the point where
the most difficult thing is not going nuts in the lich room in the
endgame watching the silly ASCII graphics at 2400 baud.

If you make polypiling affect, say, the top 5 items of the pile, and make
wands of wishing, say, be unrechargable or have a max of 1 charge, and
make rings of conflict give monsters, say, a 50% chance each round of
attacking each other, you still have all the tricks, but you've
improved the balance of the game immensely.
